ROOT — REMOVING THE GENERIC IID OPTIMIZATION DEPENDENCY
7 October2026 UTC. Composition of separately derived and audited interfaces.
No new execution or priority claim. The historical generic-I2 proof is retained.

1. Exact imported domain
The closed sharp theorem and negative-delta Gaussian filter put every true
conditional symmetric Dicke law in the coherent iid cone, for all rational
alpha>=0, delta<=2log2 and finite rational h. The direct filtered compiler
has explicit rational sector columns, polynomial-precision scalar acquisition,
a charged polynomial rational LP, and controlled conditional-type probabilities.

2. The replacement must use TRUE conditional probabilities
For each(k,u), form the rational exponents
 e_l=-delta(l+u-N/2)^2/N+h(l+u-N/2), l=0,...,k.
Pass this explicit absolute-probability acquisition procedure to the universal
regularized compiler. Max subtraction and negative-exponent clipping acquire
every normalized probability to P bits with polynomial(N,input bits,P) work.
The separability promise applies to the TRUE exponential law. It need not
apply to a rounded rational population vector. Do not silently give the new
promised-input compiler the old generic-I2 solver's rounded target.

3. Error ledger
In DIRECT_FILTERED_COMPILER.txt Section5, replace the generic I2 call by a
universal regularized call with requested accuracy eps/64. Format I has state
error <=eps/256 and Format II has <=eps/128, each smaller than the old
3eps/128 conditional-block allowance. Every other term in that direct proof
is unchanged. Its conservative18eps/256 total bound therefore still holds.
The old intermediate rounded PSD orbit target and nearest-iid optimization
are unnecessary in this replacement. k0 is an empty product.

4. Structured intermediate output for physical-spin projection
Before final local-density or finite-sampling rounding, retain Format I:
rational positive quadrature weights and rational population nodes, with exact
algebraic pure factors and the(k+1)-root-of-unity phase grid. Combine with the
exact rational positive outer(k,u) probabilities and UNIFORM virtual placement.
The result is a polynomial-label mixture of coherent/zero/one assignment laws,
exactly the input D1 of PROJECTION_DP_COMPILER.txt. It has at mostO(N^4)
outer labels; the exponentially many placements remain implicit.

For this intermediate object, omit approximate subset/string sampling and
the final dyadic rounding: these are output procedures, not prerequisites for
the positive rational mixture. Removing those error terms only improves the
target bound. The projection DP samples the posterior count law directly and
charges its own final finite-bit categorical and physical-vector rounding.

5. Cost and implementation boundary
At mostO(N^2) regularized moment compilers run, each polynomial in its degree,
input bits and log1/eps. The remaining optimization is an explicit rational
linear program with the admitted polynomial Turing algorithm/radii. No
generic multivariate real quantifier elimination or nearest-iid oracle is
needed by this stronger theoretical composition. The practical N64 code is
still its separately bounded numerical proposer with exact final certificate;
it did not execute this entire universal backend.

For heterogeneous spins, N here becomes numerical M=2sum_i j_i, the virtual
accuracy is reduced byO(M) extra bits, and the physical projection proof
charges the resulting DP and local output dimensions. Use the exact field
sign conversion in that proof's composition receipt; its physical Dicke basis
and the qubit frontend choose opposite standard z labels.

This composition does not prove a new separability domain. It compiles an
already proved promised state. Exact membership, acquisition, numerical
proposals, posterior certification and hardware preparation remain distinct.
